{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Were it not the vexation of the enemy, etc.</b> The meaning is that the enemies have provoked Me with many, many vexations. This is what is meant by ״אָגוּר״ — from the root of (Proverbs 6:8) ״אָגְרָה בַקָּצִיר״ — for the enemy's vexation is stored up and stands ready for their destruction. And when they see that I have made the name of Israel cease, heaven forfend, ״their adversaries shall misjudge״ — meaning, they will reckon that the faith of Israel is foreign and not true, and a word of truth will be reinforced as falsehood, heaven forfend. And further He is concerned ״lest they say, Our hand is exalted״ — meaning, besides their denying the faith of Israel and their religion, they will add sin by saying that their faith is a worthy faith, and that their well-being and tranquility come not from HaShem but from the idolatry that they worship." "<b>And this is</b> what is meant by <b>and that YHWH did not do all this</b> — meaning, all the good and success that they have. And the proof that Israel did nothing wrong is that they did not do [it], and furthermore they ruled over them and destroyed them." "<b>Or</b> it may intend that all this deed that they performed — causing great destruction in Israel and making the memory of man cease — they will say that YHWH did not do all this except in combination with the power and will of idol worship, which empowered them over them:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:32.160406437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}